    "title": "Google AI Mode Can Now Connect and Interact With Select Apps",
    "category": "technology",
    "categoryLabel": "Technology",
    "icon": "💻",
    "date": "2026-07-16",
    "readTime": "7 min",
    "topic": "googlesoftware",
    "slug": "google-ai-mode-connects-interacts-select-apps",
    "dek": "Google expanded AI Mode's capabilities so it can work with certain apps and deliver more useful answers within a single query.",
    "image": "img/temas/google-ai-mode-connects-interacts-select-apps.jpg",
    "videoUrl": "",
    "trending": false,
    "body": "In a significant update aimed at transforming the search experience, Google has enhanced its AI Mode to now incorporate interactions with certain apps directly. This expansion allows the search engine to process more intricate queries by bridging data from compatible services alongside standard search responses. \n\n## Streamlining User Experience\n\nTraditionally, conducting a search on Google could involve a laborious process where users had to exit the search engine and navigate to various applications to gather comprehensive information. The newly launched AI Mode addresses this issue by allowing users to extract information and receive contextual recommendations all within a single query. \n\nThis means that rather than opening separate pages or apps, users can engage with integrated functionalities seamlessly. For instance, one could initiate a search about a specific topic and immediately receive data and suggestions from apps that the AI is currently able to connect with. By creating a more unified platform, Google is taking strides towards enhancing the user experience significantly.  \n\n## Shaping the Future of Search\n\nThis update signifies a pivotal shift in the concept of what search engines can achieve. Historically, Google’s primary role revolved around presenting links to different sources; now, it aspires to become a facilitator that simplifies user inquiries and effectively assists in completing various tasks. This evolution echoes a broader trend in the tech industry, where companies, including Google, are realizing the potency of integrating smarter AI capabilities into everyday tools.  \n\nWith the capability to understand user needs more intuitively, Google aims to blend search functionality with actionable insights. A user’s general query could trigger responses interwoven with information from an app, effectively reducing the number of steps involved in obtaining the desired content. This effort resonates strongly with various sectors of the digital economy, including online shopping, content consumption, and information retrieval. \n\n## Addressing Privacy Concerns\n\nHowever, this integration does not come without its set of challenges. The synergy between the search engine and third-party applications raises considerable concerns regarding privacy. As users are encouraged to integrate their applications into their Google searches, they must also be vigilant about managing permissions and understanding how their data is being utilized. \n\nIt is imperative that individuals review what apps are linked to their Google accounts and scrutinize the permissions granted to these applications. Google users should take the initiative to ensure they comprehend the privacy settings available within their accounts, as well as ascertain how much information the AI can access in delivering more personalized answers. This aspect is crucial in building trust in the updating AI integration. \n\n## Navigating Competitive Terrain\n\nAs Google sharpens its AI capabilities, it finds itself in a competitive arena filled with other tech giants who are also advancing their own smart assistants. The ability to connect with various applications will emerge as a vital feature in this new wave of artificial intelligence services. \n\nThe effectiveness of AI Mode will be determined by several factors: how accurate and relevant the answers are, the breadth of compatible applications, and the degree of trust users place in the overall system. As tech companies race to evolve their product offerings, Google’s new AI Mode can potentially set a standard for search interactions, influencing how users expect to engage with technology moving forward.\n\nIn conclusion, Google’s AI Mode marks an innovative step towards an integrated and streamlined approach to searching and task execution, heralding changes that could redefine user interactions with search engines in a digital age increasingly reliant on automation and artificial intelligence. This update could be a linchpin in how future AI systems interact with everyday applications, shaping the broader tech landscape in the process.\n\n[publicidad]\n\n## Who the launch partners actually are\n\nAI Mode's app connections launched with exactly three partners: Instacart (for shopping and checkout), Canva (design templates) and YouTube Music (saving playlists). The rollout is US-only for now, with Google saying it plans to add more app integrations later. Google has framed the feature as a competitive answer to similar app integrations in ChatGPT and Claude.",
    "href": "categoria/technology/google-ai-mode-connects-interacts-select-apps.html",
    "sourceUrl": "https://techcrunch.com/2026/07/16/googles-ai-mode-now-lets-you-link-and-interact-with-select-apps/",
    "noindex": false,
    "correctionNote": "Corregido 2026-09-10: se nombraron los tres socios de lanzamiento (Instacart, Canva, YouTube Music), se aclaro que el lanzamiento es exclusivo de EE.UU. por ahora, y se agrego el contexto competitivo frente a ChatGPT y Claude, todo ausente en la version original.",
