    "dek": "Los Angeles sent outfielder Zyhir Hope and pitchers River Ryan and Brady Smith to Detroit in an August 2 trade for the two-time Cy Young winner, who becomes a free agent after the season.",
    "trending": false,
    "image": "img/temas/tarik-skubal-joins-the-dodgers-analyzing-the-trade-deadline-.jpg",
    "videoUrl": "",
    "body": "## What Happened\n\nThe Los Angeles Dodgers acquired two-time Cy Young Award winner Tarik Skubal from the Detroit Tigers in a trade agreed to on Saturday, August 2, 2026, and officially announced the following day, according to <a href=\"https://www.mlb.com/news/tarik-skubal-dodgers-tigers-trade\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MLB.com</a>. In return, the Dodgers sent outfield prospect Zyhir Hope (MLB Pipeline's No. 25 overall prospect), right-hander River Ryan (No. 68 overall) and right-hander Brady Smith (the Dodgers' former No. 17 prospect) to Detroit.\n\n## Skubal's Situation\n\nSkubal will be a free agent after the 2026 season; he won a $32 million arbitration ruling in February 2026. That timeline means the Dodgers are trading for what could be a single postseason run with Skubal unless they re-sign him afterward.\n\n## What Was Said\n\n\"I'm excited to be a Dodger,\" Skubal said. \"I'm excited to get down there and meet all those guys and chase three championships in a row.\" Dodgers president of baseball operations Andrew Friedman explained the front office's approach: \"There just aren't that many star-level players in the game, and any time one is available, we're always going to participate in those conversations.\"\n\n## VexlowHQ's Take\n\nThe return package -- two of the players sent to Detroit rank in the sport's top 70 prospects -- suggests the Tigers prioritized future talent over an immediate postseason push, consistent with a team further from championship contention than the reigning champion Dodgers. Whether the trade succeeds for Los Angeles depends less on the return package than on Skubal's performance in the 2026 postseason, since he can leave as a free agent regardless of outcome.\n\n## Correcting the Record\n\nThe previous version of this article named no return package, no date, and no quotes despite claiming to \"analyze\" the trade. This version adds the confirmed players exchanged, Skubal's contract status, and on-record quotes from Skubal and Friedman.",
